WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.001
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:04.837
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:06.439
That sounded so good.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:10.009
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:11.343
Everyone is talking about this.

00:00:11.343 --> 00:00:14.180
Yesterday, billionaire
Richard Branson went to space

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.683
on one of his
Virgin Galactic rockets.

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:20.820
Branson's trip to space
only lasted about four minutes,

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.855
which is honestly
pretty good for a virgin.

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:29.496
And, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:31.597
That's right.
Virgin Galactic made history

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:34.133
by launching
the first goatee into space.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.204
You know these are crazy times
when it's safer flying to space

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.906
than going on a Carnival cruise,
don't you think?

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.841
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.576
Yeah, Branson went
with two pilots

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.544
and three of his employees.

00:00:45.544 --> 00:00:47.580
So if you think it's awkward
riding an elevator

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.382
with your boss,
try going to space.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.985
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.420
That's right,
the flight went more than

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.989
50 miles high
to the edge of space.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.558
Southwest heard and was like,
"Big deal.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.960
We did that last week when one
of our pilots fell asleep."

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.965
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.301
"And look to your left, you can
see the curvature of the Earth."

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:11.370
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.939
Actually, I got a little choked
up watching Branson's flight.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:15.607
It always warms my heart
to see billionaires

00:01:15.607 --> 00:01:16.843
achieve their dreams.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:21.347
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:25.284
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.284 --> 00:01:29.054
He bought a planet!
He bought a planet!

00:01:29.054 --> 00:01:30.756
He always wanted to buy one
and he bought one,

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:33.092
bought a planet.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.260
But I was happy for him, though.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.062
Normally when a billionaire
flies away faster

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.330
than the speed of sound,

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.299
it's 'cause they just got linked
to Jeffrey Epstein.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:42.201
So, you know...
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:43.936
-Oh! Oh!
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:46.339
-Oh! Oh!
-Wow!

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.408
-Isn't live comedy fun?

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.776
Isn't it great?
Come on.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.243
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's what I'm talking about.

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:54.113
That's what I love.

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:56.683
I love you guys.
It was a pretty cool moment.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.418
I was a little surprised
by that one part, though.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.852
Did you see this?
Watch this.

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:02.321
-Three, two, one.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:04.090
Release, release, release.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.258
Ignition.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.061
Good rocket motor burn.

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.228
Everything's looking
really good in space.

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.330
[ Laughter ]
-Just a little...

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.932
Come on.
You don't need to do that.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:16.302
-There's no need.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.205
-That's right, Branson beat
Jeff Bezos to space.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.240
That's why Branson got home
and found a little flaming

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.909
Amazon package
on his front porch.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.143
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:25.979
"Ew! Who would
do something like that?"

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:30.616
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:33.119
Some political news.
Yesterday in Dallas,

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:36.289
former President Trump
gave a speech at CPAC,

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.990
where he said
that he didn't change

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.794
after being impeached twice
but actually became worse.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.395
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:45.197
Oh, my God,
he's becoming self-aware.

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:48.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.370
That's going to be
a great campaign slogan

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.939
for Trump in 2024 --
"Yep, I'm even worse."

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:55.641
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:57.376
Hey, this is fun.
I saw that President Obama

00:02:57.376 --> 00:03:00.279
just released his annual
summer reading list.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:02.047
And not to be outdone,
President Biden

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:03.816
released his own
recommendations.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.718
Here, check these out.
Obama recommends

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:08.387
"The Sweetness of Water,"
by Nathan Harris,

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:10.189
while Biden recommends
"The Crick

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:13.059
by Ol' Mary Walters' Barn,"
by Gil Lee.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:15.861
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:17.396
-Crick.

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:18.630
-It sounds like an older book,
but whatever.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.167
-An older book, yeah.
-Check out another one.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.303
Obama recommends
"Empire of Pain,"

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:26.639
by Patrick Radden Keefe,
while Biden recommends

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.107
an owner's manual
for a '74 Pontiac Firebird

00:03:29.107 --> 00:03:32.411
he found at the back of a
bargain bin at Two-Toe Hutch's

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:35.714
Antique Depot
in Fairborn, Ohio.

00:03:35.714 --> 00:03:37.350
He has two toes.
-Two-Toe.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:41.787
-And finally, Obama recommends
"Intimacies," by Katie Kitamura,

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.122
while Biden recommends

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.558
"The Official Rulebook
for Woodchuck Bowling,"

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.726
which is where you chase
a greased-up woodchuck

00:03:47.726 --> 00:03:50.095
around an alley
till it knocks down every pin.

00:03:50.095 --> 00:03:51.531
First team
to knock them all down,

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:53.333
you get to throw the woodchuck
at the other team.

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:57.069
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]
What are you talking about?

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:59.338
I've never heard of that.

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:02.675
But it's good to know
they're both readers.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.110
Hey, some business news tonight.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:07.312 line:0%
Thousands of Subway locations
across the country shut down

00:04:07.312 --> 00:04:11.717 line:0%
for a "refresh break"
to prepare for their new menu.

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:14.787
Yep.
They're on a refresh break.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.589
Sounds like something
a celebrity couple would say

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.658
instead of "We broke up."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.927
"We're on a refresh break."

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.361
That's right,
Subway closed tonight

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:25.231
and used the time to pluck
all the feathers off the tuna.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:29.769
[ Laughter ]
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:32.371
-Oh.
Ho-ho!

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.740
-This is amazing, though.
I saw that the deepest

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.410
swimming pool in the world
just opened in Dubai.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.680
It's 196 feet deep.
Check this thing out.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:50.490 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.491
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:57.396 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:57.396 --> 00:05:00.132
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:02.101
-[ Chuckles ]

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.837
-Meanwhile the ocean was like,
"You guys know I exist, right?

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.972
I mean, you can just go --"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:08.474
"You guys want to play chess
down there?

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.610
I don't know."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.511
Get this.
Nearly 200 people who paid

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:15.414
to spend the night at a zoo
in Nebraska

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:17.917
have been exposed
to a rabid bat.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:20.385
[ Laughter ]
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:05:20.385 --> 00:05:22.688
[ Laughter continues ]

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:25.591
The zoo apologized
and offered everyone a free trip

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:28.661
to the next sleepover location,
a lab in Wuhan.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:33.199
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:35.434
We can do a sleepover trip.

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:37.737
[ Laughs ]

00:05:37.737 --> 00:05:39.705
A rabid bat.

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:42.374
And, finally, a man in Michigan
was redoing his stairs

00:05:42.374 --> 00:05:45.711
when he found 160 bowling balls
under his house.

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:47.246
Look at this thing.

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:49.181
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:51.250
160 bowling balls,
and he still couldn't find

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.819
a 13-pound one
that fits his hand.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.089
Well, guys, I'm so excited
about this.

00:05:56.089 --> 00:06:00.893
The biggest band in the world,
BTS, is on the show tonight!

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:04.196
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:04.196 --> 00:06:05.698
Seriously,
you know you've made it

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.800
when you can order yourself
at McDonald's.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:11.070
Yeah? "Hi. We'll have the us.
Thank you."

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.271
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:13.639
Speaking of
the biggest pop stars,

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.575
let's get to some news.
I saw that tomorrow,

00:06:15.575 --> 00:06:18.143
Olivia Rodrigo
is going to the White House,

00:06:18.143 --> 00:06:19.511 line:0%
and she's going to team up

00:06:19.511 --> 00:06:21.814 line:0%
with President Biden
and Dr. Fauci

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:24.250 line:0%
to make videos
about getting vaccinated.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.252
Yeah.

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:29.621
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:31.691
When his staff suggested

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:33.392
bringing in
popular musical artists,

00:06:33.392 --> 00:06:34.760
Biden was like, "Great idea.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.929
How about Glenn Miller
or the Andrews Sisters?"

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:40.766
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:43.569
[ Up-tempo swing music plays ]

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.071
♪ Get your shot today ♪

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:47.306
No. I'm kidding.

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.809
Biden loves Olivia Rodrigo,
but he sings it like,

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:53.312
♪ I got my driver's license
63 years ago ♪

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:55.448
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.448 --> 00:06:57.917
Speaking of vaccines,
yesterday, a record number

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.852
of French citizens
booked appointments

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:02.321
after President Emmanuel Macron
said

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:05.591
you need to be vaccinated
to go to cafes.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:08.093
-Ew.
-That's right.

00:07:08.093 --> 00:07:11.830
French people were like, "If it
is for health, we will do it."

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:15.233
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:15.233 --> 00:07:17.570
So I guess French people
were like,

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.239
"Get vaccinated
to protect my family? Non.

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:22.308
To eat goose liver
with strangers? Oui."

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:24.109
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.109 --> 00:07:26.312
Some more news here.
According to a new book,

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:29.582
early on election night, while
votes were still coming in,

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:34.153 line:0%
Rudy Giuliani got drunk and
told Trump just to say he won.

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:37.957 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:40.359
-Yeah.

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:42.961
-Yeah, and if that didn't work,
Rudy's other plan was

00:07:42.961 --> 00:07:45.464
for Trump to legally change
his name to Joe Biden.

00:07:45.464 --> 00:07:48.601
He's like, "Boss, you did it!
You won! You're the president!"

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.769
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:53.105
That's right, Rudy was in
rough shape on election night.

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:54.940
He was slurring, sweating,
confused.

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.976
Then, he started drinking.

00:07:56.976 --> 00:07:58.477
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.477 --> 00:08:02.081 line:0%
Some business news -- the FCC
just gave Amazon the green light

00:08:02.081 --> 00:08:05.951 line:0%
to make a device that can
remotely monitor people's sleep.

00:08:05.951 --> 00:08:08.421 line:0%
-Ew.
[ Audience groans ]

00:08:08.421 --> 00:08:10.590
Right, now Amazon's like, "Yeah,

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:13.626
now we'll start
watching you sleep.

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:16.228
[ Chuckles evilly ]
Yeah."

00:08:16.228 --> 00:08:18.764
It's gonna be creepy
when Alexa is like...

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:20.366
-You're beautiful
when you sleep.

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:23.101
-That's weird. That's weird.
That's weird.

00:08:23.101 --> 00:08:25.804
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:25.804 --> 00:08:28.941
If you think this is strange,
just before you nod off,

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:31.343
a hologram of Jeff Bezos
kisses you good night

00:08:31.343 --> 00:08:33.913
on the forehead.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:33.913 --> 00:08:36.816
[ Whispering ] "Good night,
little angel."

00:08:36.816 --> 00:08:38.317
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:40.419
[ Normal voice ] Okay, so, he
sees you when you're sleeping.

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:43.088
He knows when you're awake.

00:08:43.088 --> 00:08:45.258
And he delivers gifts.

00:08:45.258 --> 00:08:47.392
Uh, Mom, Dad,
you can just tell me.

00:08:47.392 --> 00:08:48.994
Is Jeff Bezos Santa Claus?

00:08:48.994 --> 00:08:51.363
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:51.363 --> 00:08:53.098
Some entertainment news.

00:08:53.098 --> 00:08:55.301
During last night's episode of
"The Bachelorette,"

00:08:55.301 --> 00:08:58.303
Katie introduced a new challenge
for the guys.

00:08:58.303 --> 00:08:59.505
Listen to this.

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:02.174
-I kinda had this idea
that would be fun...

00:09:02.174 --> 00:09:04.676
-Okay.
-...where the guys in the house

00:09:04.676 --> 00:09:11.183
all have to agree to withhold
their self-care

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:14.553
as long as possible,
if you know what I mean.

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:15.921
-So, like, not do
their skin-care routine?

00:09:15.921 --> 00:09:17.122
-Like, no shaving?

00:09:17.122 --> 00:09:18.958
-No, we're going a little deeper
than that.

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:24.596
Even a little friendly handshake
with themselves are off limits.

00:09:24.596 --> 00:09:26.632
-Oh.
-Oh.

00:09:26.632 --> 00:09:30.135
[ Laughter ]

00:09:30.135 --> 00:09:33.172
-Ugh.
I just threw up in my mouth.

00:09:33.172 --> 00:09:34.573
-Yeah.
-What is that?

00:09:34.573 --> 00:09:36.942
Friendly handshake
with themselves?

00:09:36.942 --> 00:09:38.944
The weird thing is, it's one of
those long handshakes.

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:41.847
It's like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:44.917
Pbht.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.917 --> 00:09:47.586
Awful.

00:09:47.586 --> 00:09:49.722
Apparently Katie got tired

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:51.323
of knocking on
the Fantasy Suite door

00:09:51.323 --> 00:09:52.992
and hearing,
"Don't come in here!"

00:09:52.992 --> 00:09:54.393
[ Laughter ]

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:56.562
That's right, Katie said
that she wants all the guys

00:09:56.562 --> 00:09:59.732
to refrain from being romantic
with themselves.

00:09:59.732 --> 00:10:02.034
So, let's see how that's going
for them.

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:05.471
[ Laughter ]

00:10:05.471 --> 00:10:08.908
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:13.412 --> 00:10:15.513
[ Laughter ]
-Got to leave.

00:10:15.513 --> 00:10:17.950
-Alright, there you go.
It's an interesting episode.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.186
[ Applause ]

00:10:22.988 --> 00:10:26.525
I saw that, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:10:26.525 --> 00:10:29.762
I saw that Kraft and Van Leeuwen
teamed up

00:10:29.762 --> 00:10:31.496
to release new limited-edition

00:10:31.496 --> 00:10:33.999
macaroni-and-cheese
flavored ice cream.

00:10:33.999 --> 00:10:35.801
Look at this.

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:37.302
[ Audience groans ]

00:10:37.302 --> 00:10:39.671
That's great 'cause now I can
stop freezing Velveeta pouches

00:10:39.671 --> 00:10:41.407
and eating them like Popsicles.

00:10:41.407 --> 00:10:43.742
[ Laughter ]

00:10:43.742 --> 00:10:45.510
And finally,
officials in Minnesota

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:48.313
are asking residents
not to release their pet fish

00:10:48.313 --> 00:10:50.750
into the wild after they found

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.719
football-sized goldfish
in a local lake.

00:10:53.719 --> 00:10:55.020
This is real.
Take a look at this.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:58.757
[ Audience gasps ]
It's so big,

00:10:58.757 --> 00:11:01.494
the Discovery Channel announced
next week will be Goldfish Week.

00:11:01.494 --> 00:11:03.128
[ Laughter ]

00:11:03.128 --> 00:11:05.063
Seriously, you flush
your goldfish down the toilet,

00:11:05.063 --> 00:11:06.832
then a week later,
he knocks on the door,

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:08.734
"It's not that easy, Brian."

00:11:08.734 --> 00:11:10.602
[ Applause ]

00:11:10.602 --> 00:11:12.337
The Olympics start next week,

00:11:12.337 --> 00:11:14.205
and it was just announced
that due to COVID,

00:11:14.205 --> 00:11:17.642
Olympians will have to take
their medals off a tray

00:11:17.642 --> 00:11:21.213
and placed them
around their own necks.

00:11:21.213 --> 00:11:23.348
And just like your neighbor's
house on Halloween,

00:11:23.348 --> 00:11:25.818
the tray will have a giant sign
that says, "Please take one."

00:11:25.818 --> 00:11:27.386
[ Laughter ]

00:11:27.386 --> 00:11:28.921
